  "description": "**What `min`, `max` and `Field min/max` actually do on a relations panel** \u2014 the evidence for keeping them registered. No relations code reads any of the three directly, which makes them look inert; they are not. Grafana's `applyFieldOverrides` turns them into `field.state.range`, and that range is the domain `field.display(value)` scales against in `colorOf` \u2014 the family's only colour path. So they are the one way to pin the domain a **percentage** threshold grades against, and the only way to stop a mark's colour depending on what its neighbours happened to measure. Every panel uses the same two queries and the same percentage steps (50% / 80%); only the domain differs. Gating these three on the colour scheme being by-value needs Grafana 13.3 \u2014 see `todo/relations-conditional-field-config.md`, which names this dashboard as its verification fixture.",
