    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "1 \u2014 Percentage thresholds, no domain set",
      "description": "**The baseline.** Colour scheme `thresholds`, steps at 50% and 80% **percentage**, and neither `min` nor `max` set.\n\nWith no domain, Grafana infers one from the data: `applyFieldOverrides` computes `field.state.range` across **every field in the response**, here `[10, 90]`. Each node's median is then graded inside that shared band \u2014 `gateway` 20 \u2192 12%, `api` 55 \u2192 56%, `db` 85 \u2192 94%, `cache` 35 \u2192 31%. So one green, one yellow, one red, one green.\n\nThe catch this dashboard exists to show: the band is whatever the data happened to be, so a node's colour changes when an **unrelated** node's numbers change.",
