      "id": 2,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "2 \u2014 Explicit min / max pins the domain",
      "description": "**`min: 0`, `max: 100` \u2014 the same data, graded against a domain the author chose.**\n\n`gateway` 20%, `api` 55%, `db` 85%, `cache` 35%. Two of the four cross a different step than in panel 1, and \u2014 the actual point \u2014 these colours no longer move when a neighbour's traffic does.\n\nThis is why `min`/`max` are **kept** for this family even though no relations code reads them: `applyFieldOverrides` turns them into `field.state.range`, which is the domain `field.display(value)` scales against in `colorOf` (`converters/markRead.ts`) \u2014 the only colour path relations has. They are the one way to pin a percentage-threshold domain.",
