      "id": 3,
      "type": "grafana-echartsrelations-panel",
      "title": "3 \u2014 Field min/max grades each mark against itself",
      "description": "**`fieldMinMax: true`, and it does something unmistakable: all four nodes turn yellow.**\n\nOn, each field's range is computed from **that field alone** instead of across the whole response. Every node's samples straddle its own median \u2014 `gateway` is `[10, 30]` with median 20, `db` is `[80, 90]` with median 85 \u2014 so every mark sits at 50% of its own range and lands on the same step. Compare against panels 1, 2 and 4, each of which paints at least one node red or green.\n\nThat is the honest answer to \"does Field min/max do anything here?\" \u2014 yes, and it changes the *question* the colour answers, from \"how does this node compare to the others\" to \"how does it compare to its own recent range\".",
